  "worked_solution": "Recall that the principal $12$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/12}\\ne 1,\n$$\n\nand that any $12$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,\u2026,11.$  Also, we have ${z}^{12}=1.$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of a geometric sequence, we obtain that the sum of all twelve roots is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+z+{z}^{2}+\u22ef+{z}^{11} & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-{z}^{12})}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-1)}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0}{1-z} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
